            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഒമ്പതാം (ompathāṁ) — \"ninth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഒമ്പത് was already a built word when you learned it: an old word for one plus pathŭ, ten — one short of ten, with the n turning to m before the p. The ordinal ending goes on top of that, and none of the machinery underneath reacts to it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഒമ്പതാം ദിവസം (ompathāṁ divasam), the ninth day."
            }
          ]
        },
