        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ആദ്യം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആദ്യം (ādyaṁ) — \"at first\", \"first of all\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is not another ordinal. ഒന്നാം picks an item out of a line: the first door, the first way. ആദ്യം (ādyaṁ) puts an action first in time, and it pairs with പിന്നെ, which you already have:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആദ്യം (ādyaṁ) ഊണ്, പിന്നെ ചായ. — Ādyaṁ ūṇŭ, pinne chāya. \"Lunch first, then tea.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way — the one word Malayalam borrowed here",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Notice what did and did not get borrowed. Malayalam's ordinals are native, and their ending is so regular that it never needed a special word for first — the one place its sisters all reached for മുതൽ. But for first as an adverb, the language reached into Sanskrit and took ആദ്യം (ādyaṁ), from ādya, \"primary\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So a language can have a perfect machine for one job and still borrow a word for the neighbouring one. It is worth carrying that as a habit of reading: a borrowing is evidence about a slot, not about the language as a whole."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two kinds of order, and the words for both:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "what you are ordering",
                "word"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "what you are ordering: a thing in a line. word: ഒന്നാം onnāṁ, and the ten after it.",
                "what you are ordering: an action in time. word: ആദ്യം ādyaṁ, with പിന്നെ pinne."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
